From 725630879b1f471a43942ccd9a718099bb1f20fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:00:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf(deepseek-v4.1): sequence-parallel prefill decoder
 dataflow

Stage 2 of the prefill-only sequence-parallel mode. When a forward uses SP
each rank keeps L = Tp / TP rows between collectives, where Tp = TP *
ceil(T / TP):

- The embedding reduce-scatter result stays local; inputs_embeds are sliced.
- The residual, mixes and carried layer output are local, so the mHC pre,
  post and post_pre kernels, both norms and the Engram gate run on L rows.
- Attention all-gathers its input to T rows behind the opaque attention op
  (the rows are scoped to the call with a context variable), runs every
  projection, indexer, compressor, KV cache write and sparse MLA on all
  rows as before, writes WO into a zero-padded Tp-row buffer and
  reduce-scatters it instead of the all-reduce.
- The MoE input is gathered to T rows with the full input_ids; gate, top-k,
  routed and shared experts run as before, and the runner reduce-scatters
  shared + routed from a zero-padded buffer instead of its final all-reduce,
  still firing the L2 prefetch pre-reduce hook first.
- Engram keeps its staged-row all-reduce and runs wkv on every row, then
  gates only this rank's real rows; pad rows pass through.
- The final collapse and norm run locally and are gathered to T rows, as
  are the aux hidden states a drafter consumes. DSpark reads only those, so
  its pre-collapse MTP buffer is left alone under SP; other drafters gather
  it.

Kernels never see more than T rows and gathered tensors are used as [:T].
Decode, the default path and every weight are unchanged.
